From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: opencode-port <port@localhost>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:29:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] D108 permissions: "always" on a command after assignments or
 redirects saves a pattern that matches it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Upstream: a command's resource keeps the assignments and redirects in front of it (`FOO=1 git status`), but its saved pattern was built from the words after them (`git status *`), which never matches that resource. "Always" saved an approval that could not apply, so the same command asked again every time. Upstream's own parity test skipped these resources when checking that a save matches its resource.
Fixed: when the prefix pattern does not match the command's resource, the command is saved exactly as approved (`FOO=1 git status`, `2>err git status`, `<<EOF cat …`). The same applies to a command whose words are separated by extra spaces or tabs (`git  commit   -m …` saved `git commit *`, which never matched it either). Approving `FOO=1 git status` does not approve `LD_PRELOAD=x git status`.
Scenarios: permissions.test.ts "always on a command with an environment assignment approves it under that assignment only" (new); shell-classify.test.ts assignments and declarations, heredocs, redirections, quoting and escaping (recorded save patterns)
Upstream tests: test/shell-parse-parity.test.ts (no longer skips assignment-led resources), test/shell-parse-compatibility.test.ts and test/shell-scan/redirect.test.ts (asserted saves that do not match their resource), test/shell-parse.test.ts (new test)

diff --git a/packages/core/src/shell/parse.ts b/packages/core/src/shell/parse.ts
index 54acedc788..562258a4a2 100644
--- a/packages/core/src/shell/parse.ts
+++ b/packages/core/src/shell/parse.ts
@@ -244,8 +244,12 @@ export function scan(command: string, shell: string, cwd: string): Effect.Effect
         if (directoryCommand === parts && resolved.complete) continue
       }
       const selected = powershell ? prefix(words) : bashPrefix(words)
-      // A command that only the shell can identify is saved exactly as approved.
-      const conventional = selected ? `${selected.join(" ")} *` : item.resource
+      const prefixed = selected && `${selected.join(" ")} *`
+      // A command that only the shell can identify is saved exactly as approved. So is one whose resource starts with
+      // assignments or redirects (`FOO=1 git status`): a prefix of its words would never match it, and dropping them
+      // would approve the command under any other environment.
+      const conventional =
+        prefixed && (powershell || Wildcard.match(item.resource, prefixed)) ? prefixed : item.resource
       const end = selected && item.wordEnds?.[selected.length - 1]
       // Keep existing grants stable unless normalized spacing loses the original source boundary.
       const save =
